================================================================================
HOW ONE HANDLER UPDATES MULTIPLE FIELDS
================================================================================

USER CHANGES:

First Name


event.target:

{
  name:
    'firstName',

  value:
    'John'
}


GENERIC HANDLER:

setFormData(previous => ({

  ...previous,

  value

}))


RESULT:

{
  firstName:
    'John',

  lastName:
    '',

  email:
    '',

  phone:
    ''
}


================================================================================
ANOTHER FIELD
================================================================================

User enters:

john@example.com


Input:

name="email"


Therefore:

value


becomes:

email:
'john@example.com'


Final state:

{
  firstName:
    'John',

  lastName:
    '',

  email:
    'john@example.com',

  phone:
    ''
}


================================================================================
BASIC FORM TABLE
================================================================================

+----------------------------+------------------------------------------+
| CODE                       | PURPOSE                                  |
+----------------------------+------------------------------------------+
| INITIAL_FORM               | Reusable initial state                  |
| formData                   | Current field values                    |
| setFormData                | Requests state update                   |
| name                       | Matches object property                 |
| value                      | Current input value                     |
| [name]                     | Dynamic property                        |
| ...previousData            | Preserve remaining fields              |
| preventDefault()           | Prevent native submit                  |
| onReset                    | Restore initial controlled state        |
+----------------------------+------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
IMPORTANT RESET PATTERN
================================================================================

Instead of:

<button
  type="reset"
  onClick={handleReset}
>


prefer handling the reset at the form level:

<form
  onReset={handleReset}
>


with:

<button type="reset">
  Clear
</button>


For controlled React fields, the reset handler should restore React state.

There is normally no need to call:

event.preventDefault()

just to reset controlled fields.


