================================================================================
IMPORTANT: NUMBER INPUT
================================================================================

This field:

<input
  type="number"
  name="age"
/>


still normally supplies:

event.target.value


as a STRING.


Example:

User enters:

35


event.target.value:

"35"


If the application requires a number, convert deliberately.


Example:

const nextValue =

  type === 'checkbox'
    ? checked

    : type === 'number'
      ? (
          value === ''
            ? ''
            : Number(value)
        )

      : value


Whether conversion belongs in the generic handler or at submission depends
on your desired form-state model.


