The most reusable multi-input pattern is:

const handleChange = (
  event
) => {

  const {
    name,
    value,
    type,
    checked
  } = event.target


  const nextValue =
    type === 'checkbox'
      ? checked
      : value


  setFormData(previous => ({

    ...previous,

    nextValue

  }))
}


The important connection is:

INPUT name
     ↓
MATCHES
     ↓
STATE PROPERTY


Example:

name="email"

        ↓

formData.email


This allows many related controls to share one update mechanism while
remaining predictable and easy to maintain.


